  "reason": "Evidence: Two experiments establish that RNA (PCA-2000, single profile) yields 0.485 accuracy while image (ResNet-50, single profile) yields only 0.208, confirming RNA as the dominant signal. However, we have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the RNA branch. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether aggregating multiple profiles (here via avgpool) with the same PCA-2000 encoder meaningfully improves over the single-profile baseline, and this axis (profile setting + aggregation) is orthogonal to encoder choice and will affect the design of all downstream multimodal configurations. This experiment (config_002) changes exactly one variable from config_001—profile_setting from single to multi with avgpool aggregation—while holding encoder, modality, and fusion fixed. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation cleanly. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it directly extends the best-performing baseline, (2) a positive result validates the entire multiprofile branch (configs 003, 005-009, 018-027, etc.), while a null or negative result redirects search toward single-profile and encoder variation, and (3) it reduces uncertainty about a design axis that is shared across the majority of remaining configurations, making the result broadly informative for subsequent decisions."
}

